"Let an oriented link be a **boundary link** if its components bound pairwise disjoint Seifert surfaces in $S^3$. Let the **trivial link** be the link whose components are disjoint unknotted circles bounding disjoint disks. Two links are self $\\Delta$-equivalent when they are transformed into each other by self delta moves and ambient isotopies, with all three strings in each move belonging to the same component. **Shibuya's conjecture.** Any boundary link is self $\\Delta$-equivalent to the trivial link. This conjecture predicts that self Delta-equivalence detects no further obstruction for boundary links beyond their boundary-link structure; the supplied text gives no resolution."